2. Conveying Modified Versions of the Library.

If you modify a copy of the Library, or, in the case of a copy, you
link a copy of the Library with it, you must, at the same time, provide
through all the copies of the Library a copy of this License for all
the Library, as follows:

    a) Each copy of the Library must be accompanied by a copy of this
    License.

    b) You must ensure that the recipient is informed that this License
    applies to the Library and how they can obtain a copy of this
    License.

    c) You must ensure that the recipient receives a copy of this License,
    or is provided with a copy of this License, and that they are
    informed that they can obtain the Corresponding Source for the Library
    by contacting the copyright holder or by other reasonable means.

    d) If the recipient conveys a copy of the Library with the work, the
    recipient must also convey a copy of this License for the Library.

3. Conveying Non-Source Forms of the Library.

You may convey a work in object code form under the terms of sections 3
and 4, provided that you also convey the machine-readable Corresponding
Source under the terms of this License, in one of these ways:

    a) Convey the work accompanied by the Corresponding Source.  This
    Corresponding Source must be conveyed in the form described in this
    License.

    b) Convey the work accompanied by a written offer, valid for at
    least three years and valid for as long as you offer spare parts or
    customer support for that model of product, to give anyone who
    possesses the work either (1) a copy of the Corresponding Source for
    all the software in the work that is covered by this License, and
    (2) access to copy the Corresponding Source from a network server at
    no charge.

    c) Convey the work accompanied by the information received as a
    result of providing a copy of the Corresponding Source.

4. Combined Works.

You may convey a Combined Work under the terms of your choice,
provided that you comply with the terms of this License for each of the
components of the Combined Work.

When you convey a Combined Work, you must also:

    a) Provide a copy of this License for the Library.

    b) Provide a copy of the Corresponding Source for the Library, and
    retain all notices that refer to this License and the absence of any
    warranty.

    c) If the work provides access to a user interface, you must provide
    a user interface that does not require a user to take any action
    beyond what is necessary to obtain the Corresponding Source.

    d) Include with the work a written offer, valid for at least three
    years and valid for as long as you offer spare parts or customer
    support for that model of product, to give anyone who possesses the
    work (1) a copy of the Corresponding Source for all the software in
    the work that is covered by this License, and (2) access to copy the
    Corresponding Source from a network server at no charge.

    e) If the work provides access to a user interface, you must provide
    a user interface that does not require a user to take any action
    beyond what is necessary to obtain the Corresponding Source.

5. Your License Obligations for the Library.

If you convey a copy of the Library, you must retain all notices that
refer to this License and the absence of any warranty.

If you convey a copy of the Library with a work, you must also:

    a) Include a copy of this License for the Library.

